; ── SNSP-003 RF Switch (PAL) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; PalRfSwitch, an RfSwitch with NO TV lead: the box plugs straight onto the set's
; aerial socket, so PlugB0 IS the box (connector coax_plug: the set's F socket takes
; it; the real one is IEC). Its aerial socket is PlugB0/AntPort on the far end, and
; the console lead (PlugA0, a black phono plug, 3 m) leaves PlugB0/DeckLeadAttach on
; the box's side. No Body, no TvRope; the one rope is VerletRope (CompositeCable's
; name for it).
;
; ── The frame ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; PlugB0's frame is a plug's: the connector along +Z, the MATING plane at the origin
; (a seated plug stands at zone * R_x(180), its SnapGrabPoint). RetroXR-models'
; nintendo/snes/rf-switch-pal GLB (glTF: meters, +Y up, back face on y = 0, box
; 25.7 x 18 x 35.2 centered in X and Z, the barrel along +Z with its tip at
; TVPlugAnchor (0, 0.009, 0.0273)) has its mating plane on the face the barrel
; leaves, z = 0.0176 (the tip less the barrel's 9.7 mm), on the barrel's axis:
;
;   p_PlugB0 = p_glTF - (0, 0.009, 0.0176)
;   i.e. Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, -0.009, -0.0176)   (.tscn rows)
;
; A pure translation: the stock set's RfPort zone is R_x(180) off the set, so a
; seated plug's frame is the set's own and the box stands upright (glTF +Y up).
; The model's empties, mapped:
;   TVPlugAnchor      (0, 0.009, 0.0273)       -> (0, 0, 0.0097), the barrel's tip
;   AntennaAnchor     (0, 0.009, -0.0206)      -> AntPort (0, 0, -0.0382), basis
;                     R_x(180): the zone's +Z faces PlugB0 -Z, where an aerial plug
;                     arrives from, and the plug seats moving +Z
;   ConsoleCordAnchor (0.02535, 0.009, -0.0124) -> DeckLeadAttach (0.02535, 0, -0.03),
;                     R_y(-90): the rope leaves along its local -Z = +X
;
; ── For a mod that dresses it ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
; PlugB0/Shell holds every stand-in mesh and IS the glTF frame (its transform is the
; one above, its children in the model's own numbers): hide it and add the GLB under
; PlugB0 at that transform. Set PlugB0/AntPort's show_jack false if the model
; moulds its socket.
[node name="PalRfSwitch" type="Node3D"]
script = ExtResource("1_switchscript")
cord_colors = PackedColorArray(0.07, 0.07, 0.08, 1)

; ── End B: the box ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[node name="PlugB0" type="RigidBody3D" parent="."]
